# npm is the package manager for this repo (package-lock.json is the tracked
# lockfile; workspaces are npm workspaces). Lockfiles/artifacts from bun and pnpm
# are side effects of a tool that is not part of the toolchain and must never be
# committed — a third lockfile silently wins on some machines and installs a
# different tree than CI does.
bun.lock
bun.lockb
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
node_modules/.pnpm/

# `patch`/`git apply` leftovers: a rejected hunk leaves these beside the target.
*.orig
*.rej

# One-off investigation scratch space. Anything here is a single-sighting probe
# by definition; real tools get promoted into tools/ and committed from there.
scratch/

# shadcn-svelte's config, present at apps/web/components.json only. It is not
# junk by accident: it points at src/lib/components/ui, src/lib/utils.ts and
# tailwind.config.js, and NONE of those exist here — there is no components/ui
# directory, no utils.ts, no tailwind config file at all, and neither shadcn-svelte
# nor bits-ui is a dependency (this app is Tailwind v4 via the Vite plugin, which
# has no config file for it to name).
#
# It is therefore config for a setup this repo does not have, and every path in
# it is wrong. Committing it would be worse than ignoring it: `npx
# shadcn-svelte add` reads it to decide where to write components, so it would
# scatter new files into a directory tree the build never reads. If shadcn is
# adopted for real, delete this line and commit the config the tool generates.
apps/web/components.json

